Mon Oct 26 11:20:58 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.13.1 (upstream tag v0.13.1, 2026-10-25):
  * Edit: fix source offset when trimming the start of a stretched
    audio clip; heal keeps each clip's gain envelope and skips clips
    whose mute or stretch differ; deleting fades leaves unrelated
    overlapping clips untouched; MIDI note selection stays valid
    across clip, session and note-order changes.
  * Tracks: track and group names are clipped to their rows in the
    side lists; track-name collisions after truncation are
    prevented; exact channel formats are preserved when committing
    tracks.
  * Audio I/O: Float32 WAV and AIFF-C encoding keeps finite
    headroom; the full WAVE_FORMAT_EXTENSIBLE fmt chunk is
    validated; older sessions with a bare Fit track height load.
  * VST3 host: IMessage and IAttributeList are provided to plugins.
  * automation.clip_gain_to_volume keeps the existing volume lane;
    the Record button tooltip names F12.
  * Re-vendored with update=true (cargo-dependencies group bump).
    License audit: no new copyleft in the Linux targets (only
    Windows/UEFI-only crates carry BSL-1.0 or LGPL options), so the
    License tag and the Legal-Review-Notice are unchanged. No new
    system deps.
- Set the fixed AppStream release date to 2026-10-25 (v0.13.1).

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Oct 23 06:51:32 UTC 2026 - Paolo Stivanin <info@paolostivanin.com>

- Update to 0.12.1 (upstream tag v0.12.1, 2026-10-22):
  * 0.11.0 is a version-only release (CI config, no code changes);
    0.12.0 was never tagged, and 0.12.1 only adds a macOS
    notarisation stapler retry on top of it.
  * Edit: bare "=" nudges the selected clip right, matching "-";
    the playlist stays sorted after delete_fades trims overlapping
    clips; automation writes keep the breakpoint at end + 1.
  * Mix: mix.send to an unknown bus name is rejected instead of
    creating a bus; normalize no longer produces inf samples for
    subnormal peaks.
  * Hardening: integer-overflow fixes in the tempo map, timecode
    frame counts and pan automation labels; undefined SMPTE frame
    rates in MIDI headers and zero/invalid NAL length widths in
    video bitstreams are rejected.
  * Re-vendored with update=true: no crates added or removed, only
    version bumps (icu_* 2.4.0, memmap2 0.9.12, tinystr 0.8.5,
    webbrowser 1.2.5, yoke 0.8.4, zerovec 0.11.9, plus clipboard-win,
    open and tokio, which the Linux targets do not link). License
    audit: every bumped crate keeps its licence, no new copyleft,
    so the License tag and the Legal-Review-Notice are unchanged.
    No new system deps; MSRV still 1.90. cargo_audit reports no
    advisories.
- Set the fixed AppStream release date to 2026-10-22 (v0.12.1); it
  was still the v0.8.0 date.

