Thu Oct 15 05:04:24 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.7.0 (upstream tag v0.7.0):
  * Edit: Shuffle/Slip/Spot/Grid modes, Pencil/Grabber MIDI clips,
    transient detection with Tab to Transient, clip fades with live
    waveform previews, Consolidate over the selection.
  * Mix: separate Mix window, Pro Tools-like tracks/slots/faders,
    delay compensation on masters and aux bounces, VST3/CLAP safety.
  * Engine: crash recovery with unsaved-work offer, corrupt files and
    sessions refused instead of crashing, bounded control-server
    requests, no audio-thread allocs, streamed disk bounces.
  * UI: Silver Light theme, track tinting, grid over clips, Send levels
    to -inf, marker double-click rename, Hangul fallback font.
  * Files: .m4b audiobooks, File Open Recent, Signal Generator fills
    selection, MCP file-access confinement flags.
  * Re-vendor with update=true (craft-ui git dep still needed);
    license audit finds no new copyleft (MPL-2.0 symphonia and
    Apache-2.0-option self_cell as before), so the License tag is
    unchanged. No CVEs in the v0.6.1 to v0.7.0 range.
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 13 07:32:10 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.6.1:
  * New built-in Sampler instrument; record takes straight to
    disk.
  * Save safety: copies without retargeting, never overwrite
    audio or sessions, synced saves with backups, prompt on
    unsaved changes.
  * Edit window: fixed drag selection, trackpad panning with
    pinch and Cmd+scroll zoom, Clip List management and clip
    export as files.
  * Mixer routing menus and numeric controls; instrument params
    pushed before each block; adaptive meter polling with live
    armed meters while stopped.
  * MIDI controller export honouring the tracks filter,
    multichannel import, per-file consolidation, named-bus
    bounce with unknown-bus rejection.
  * CLI: survive closed stdout, dotted command-id shorthand,
    MCP batch surfaces failures with keep_going; app sleeps
    when idle or covered.
  * Re-vendor for zip 9 (session bundles), nix, typed-path and
    the craft-ui git dependency; license audit finds no new
    copyleft, so the License tag is unchanged. No CVEs in the
    0.5.0 to 0.6.1 range.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct 11 19:16:29 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package (version 0.5.0): native digital audio
  workstation with non-destructive clip editing (fades, playlists,
  grids, markers) and a mixer with inserts, sends, buses,
  automation and metering.
- Built-in EQ, dynamics, reverb, delay, modulation and instruments;
  CLAP and VST3 plugin hosting with per-vendor menus.
- Imports WAV, AIFF, FLAC, MP3 and MIDI and bounces mixes to disk;
  the soundcraft-cli subpackage adds headless editing and an MCP
  server for scripting and agents.
- Recent highlights: clip-gain nudge, resizable MIDI dock, tempo
  operations as stretch factor, snap to neighbours, metronome click
  in live playback, Linux system fonts via fontconfig, and logging
  to stderr plus a rotating log file.

